.TH "SERIALPORT.CONNECT_EVENT" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.connect_event \- SerialPort: connect event
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]connect\f[B]\f[R] event of the \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
interface is fired when the port connects to the device.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqconnect\(dq, (event) => { })

onconnect = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH DESCRIPTION
More specifically, the \f[CR]connect\f[R] event fires when the port
becomes \f[B]logically connected\f[R] to the device.
This happens after a user grants permission for a site to access the
port that the device is attached to, following a
\f[CR]Serial.requestPort()\f[R] call:
.IP \(bu 2
In the case of a wired serial port, this occurs when the port is
physically connected to the device, for example via USB.
.IP \(bu 2
In the case of a wireless serial port (for example, Bluetooth RFCOMM),
this occurs when the port makes one or more active connections to the
device (for example via Bluetooth L2CAP channels).
.SS Bubbling
This event bubbles up to the \f[CR]Serial\f[R] instance that returned
this interface.
The \f[CR]event.target\f[R] property refers to the \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R]
object that bubbles up.
.PP
For more information, see Event bubbling.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Notify when a specific port connects
The \f[CR]Serial.requestPort()\f[R] method returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R]
that resolves with a \f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] chosen by the user.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Prompt user to choose a serial port\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] port = \f[B]await\f[R] navigator.serial.requestPort();

port.addEventListener(\(dqconnect\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// notify that the chosen port is connected\f[R]
});
.EE
.SS Listening for any newly\-connected ports
The \f[CR]connect\f[R] event bubbles up to the \f[CR]Serial\f[R] object
where you can listen for any newly\-connected ports.
.IP
.EX
navigator.serial.addEventListener(\(dqconnect\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[I]// notify that a new port is available\f[R]
  \f[I]// use \(gaevent.target\(ga to refer to the newly\-added port\f[R]
});
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]disconnect\f[R] event
